# Nginx Reverse Proxy Setup Instructions

This setup uses nginx reverse proxy on a **different server**:
1. **Front Reverse Proxy Server** (`batocera-games-catalog-reverse-proxy`) - Listens on ports 80/443, handles SSL termination
2. **Backend Server** - Has nginx serving media files and proxying API requests to FastAPI on port 8000

## Setup Steps

### 1. On the Front Reverse Proxy Server:

#### 1.1. Update backend server addresses
Edit `batocera-games-catalog-reverse-proxy` and update both upstream blocks:

```
upstream backend_nginx {
    server BACKEND_SERVER_IP:80;  # Backend nginx on port 80
}

upstream backend_api {
    server BACKEND_SERVER_IP:8000;  # FastAPI backend on port 8000
}
```

For example:
```
upstream backend_nginx {
    server 192.168.1.100:80;
    # OR
    server backend.example.com:80;
}

upstream backend_api {
    server 192.168.1.100:8000;
    # OR
    server backend.example.com:8000;
}
```

#### 1.2. Update domain name
Replace `YOUR_DOMAIN` with your actual domain name and `_` in `server_name` directives.

#### 1.3. Enable the configuration
```bash
sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/batocera-games-catalog-reverse-proxy /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
```

### 2. On the Backend Server:

The backend server should have nginx configured with:
- Serving media files from `/media/`
- Proxying `/api` requests to FastAPI on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`
- Serving static frontend files from `/`

Use the `batocera-games-catalog` configuration file (or your existing nginx config).

### 3. Setup SSL certificates (if not already done)
On the front reverse proxy server, generate certificates using certbot:
```bash
sudo certbot certonly --nginx -d your-domain.com
```

### 4. Update certificate paths
On the front reverse proxy server, update the SSL certificate paths in `batocera-games-catalog-reverse-proxy`:
```
ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/YOUR_DOMAIN/fullchain.pem;
ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/YOUR_DOMAIN/privkey.pem;
```

### 5. Test and reload nginx
On the front reverse proxy server:
```bash
# Test configuration
sudo nginx -t

# Reload nginx
sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

## Architecture

```
Internet
   |
   v
[Front Reverse Proxy Server - Different Machine]
Ports: 80 (HTTP), 443 (HTTPS)
SSL Termination
   |
   +---> /api requests → [Backend Server Port 8000] (FastAPI)
   |
   +---> All other requests → [Backend Server Port 80] (Nginx)
                                |
                                +---> Serves static files (/)
                                +---> Serves media files (/media/)
```

## Firewall Configuration

### Front Reverse Proxy Server:
- Port 80 (HTTP) - Allow from Internet
- Port 443 (HTTPS) - Allow from Internet
- Port for backend connection - Allow outbound to backend server

### Backend Server:
- Port 80 (backend nginx) - Allow from front reverse proxy server IP only
- Port 8000 (FastAPI) - Allow from front reverse proxy server IP only

## Notes

- The front reverse proxy handles SSL termination
- The connection between front proxy and backend servers can be HTTP (if on private network) or HTTPS (for better security)
- All security headers are set in the front reverse proxy
- Request routing:
  - `/api` requests are proxied directly to FastAPI on port 8000
  - All other requests (media, static files, frontend) are proxied to backend nginx on port 80
- Backend server's nginx (port 80) handles:
  - Media file serving with thumbnail resizing
  - Static frontend file serving
- FastAPI backend (port 8000) receives API requests directly from the reverse proxy
- Both backend services (nginx:80 and FastAPI:8000) should only be accessible from the front reverse proxy server IP
- Logs are separated:
  - Front proxy: `/var/log/nginx/batocera-games-catalog-reverse-proxy-*.log`
  - Backend: `/var/log/nginx/batocera-games-catalog-*.log`

